Ujson Fuzzer Setup Note
=======================
Ujson is a fast JSON encoder/decoder library written in C with Python bindings.
The fuzzer requires compilation of C extensions.

Setup completed:
- Created /app/ujson/fuzz.py with LibFuzzer-compatible fuzzer
- Created /app/ujson/notes_for_testing.txt with key functions to test
- Attempted to create virtual environment at /app/ujson/.venv

Setup status:
The ujson installation requires compilation of C extensions which was in progress.

To complete the ujson fuzzer setup:
1. Create virtual environment: python3 -m venv /app/ujson/.venv
2. Activate and install: source .venv/bin/activate && pip install -e .
3. Install atheris: pip install atheris
4. Run fuzzer: timeout 10 python3 fuzz.py > fuzz.log 2>&1

Fuzzer will test:
- ujson.loads() with malformed JSON
- ujson.dumps() with various Python objects
- Nested JSON structures
- Custom encoding options
